{
 "summary": "Implemented read-ahead buffering for hosted signed rows and the seven-parameter hostedStreamEvents API. Incoming chunks report progress; row polls do not. Buffered blocks retain Anthropic signature/stop ordering. Missing rows after completion fail transiently, and completion without a stop preserves the service error. All 16 focused tests pass, including an actual 30-second delayed-row scenario. No hidden acceptance tests ran.",
 "files_modified": [
  "src/orchestration/modules/provider-claude-agent-sdk/agent-host/agent-stream.ts",
  "src/orchestration/modules/provider-claude-agent-sdk/agent-host/agent-bridge.ts",
  "tests/unit/orchestration/modules/provider-claude-agent-sdk/agent-host/agent-stream.test.ts"
 ],
 "plan_corrections": [
  {
   "original": "Raise a block-relative bound in agent-bridge.ts because slow disks are the only defect.",
   "evidence": "The bound actually lived in agent-stream.ts. Its nextSigned loop blocked consumption of later events. The new delayed-row regression timed out against that implementation and emitted the original wrote-no-row error.",
   "implemented": "Read later events while awaiting signed rows, buffer their emission, and start the 60-second bound only after the stop chunk. Do not impose a generation-duration bound."
  },
  {
   "original": "Report progress on every row poll.",
   "evidence": "anthropic.ts:407 routes onProgress to streamLiveness.frame(); therefore poll progress would report activity even when no model chunks arrive. The new test confirms that 30 seconds of polling adds no progress callbacks.",
   "implemented": "Report progress once per received item, including items buffered behind a pending signature."
  },
  {
   "original": "Assert that the engine writes every signed row within a minute of block end.",
   "evidence": "agent-file.ts:90-128 reads appended rows but establishes no timing guarantee. host-plugin/hooks/register.js.txt:43-52 forwards chunks before yielding them back to the engine.",
   "implemented": "Removed the unsupported timing comment. The new comment describes the local post-stop timeout rather than claiming engine behavior."
  }
 ],
 "commands_run": [
  {
   "command": "bun test --preload ./tests/preload.ts ./tests/unit/orchestration/modules/provider-claude-agent-sdk/agent-host/host-gate.test.ts ./tests/unit/orchestration/modules/provider-claude-agent-sdk/agent-host/engine-text.test.ts",
   "exit_code": 0,
   "result": "Baseline: 14 tests passed."
  },
  {
   "command": "bun test --preload ./tests/preload.ts ./tests/unit/orchestration/modules/provider-claude-agent-sdk/agent-host/agent-stream.test.ts",
   "exit_code": 124,
   "result": "RED: test could not advance the input iterator while awaiting a row; test timed out and the original implementation subsequently threw wrote-no-row. Command stopped at 25 seconds."
  },
  {
   "command": "bun test --preload ./tests/preload.ts ./tests/unit/orchestration/modules/provider-claude-agent-sdk/agent-host/agent-stream.test.ts",
   "exit_code": 0,
   "result": "Initial GREEN: two tests passed."
  },
  {
   "command": "bun test --preload ./tests/preload.ts ./tests/unit/orchestration/modules/provider-claude-agent-sdk/agent-host/agent-stream.test.ts ./tests/unit/orchestration/modules/provider-claude-agent-sdk/agent-host/host-gate.test.ts ./tests/unit/orchestration/modules/provider-claude-agent-sdk/agent-host/engine-text.test.ts",
   "exit_code": 0,
   "result": "Final verification: 16 tests, 70 assertions passed, including the expanded 30-second delayed-row case."
  }
 ],
 "remaining_followups": [
  "Live Claude subscription behavior and the complete shared-adapter stall deadline were not exercised; tests establish stream buffering, event ordering, and progress callback behavior.",
  "Parent owns final review, commit, and push. No Git commands or project-wide gates ran."
 ]
}

